    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d23">

                <pb facs="0079" n="589" sameAs="frus:frus1948v05p2/pg589"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BB Palestine/2–348</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Director of the, Office of United Nations
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Rusk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the United States Representative at the United Nations</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Austin</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-02-03">February 3,
                        1948</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Senator Austin</hi>: The attached memorandum
                    contains a draft telegram on the question of the acceptance by the Security
                    Council of its responsibilities under the General Assembly Resolution on
                    Palestine. In order to avoid sending broadly phrased instructions without direct
                    reference to the problem presented to the Security Council, it was decided that
                    I should furnish you the attached draft for your information. The Department may
                    convert this draft into an instruction or it may separate out certain points
                    raised therein for more precise instructions in the light of the questions
                    presented to the Security Council.</p>
                <p>I appreciate that this is a somewhat unusual procedure but I am confident that
                    you will understand the difficulty in general instructions at this point.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dean Rusk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d23-a1.xml" xpointer="d23-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
